        "pageid": 37861841,
        "ns": 0,
        "title": "Atari Greatest Hits",
        "extract": "Atari Greatest Hits is a series of video game compilations developed by Code Mystics and published by Atari, Inc. for the Nintendo DS and iOS. Consisting of arcade and Atari 2600 games from Atari, it was released into two volumes released in 2010 and 2011 respectively, while the app was released as a free-to-play model, and allowed for purchase of the extra games.  The games include bonus features such as manuals, credits and interviews with Atari founder Nolan Bushnell.\nReleases in the series have received positive reviews from IGN and Eurogamer while receiving more negative reviews from Nintendo Power and Nintendo Gamer.\n\n",
